From 840d22ea244729221f75f09fd2c0da8751048a17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tstoltz <tristan.stoltz@evolvingresonantcocreationism.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 13:30:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Model O-provider (in-process dlopen'd C ABI; Nix owns
 native policy)

Implements the O-provider stop/go review's GO verdict: a minimal,
versioned, PKCS#11-inspired (not compliant) verification-only C ABI
for in-process signature observation providers, grounded in the real
#14451 thread's xokdvium comment. Reuses Model N's KeyGroup/
allSignatureGroupsSatisfied native-policy composition, same as
Model O-process, keeping the marginal cost (456 lines) below both H
(617) and O-process (500) despite the new in-process-ABI risk
category.

- signature-provider-abi.h: single versioned vtable, one verify() op
- signature-inprocess-provider.{hh,cc}: dlopen/dlsym wiring, cached
  for the process lifetime, never dlclosed
- local-store.hh/.cc: signature-observation-provider-{library,mode,
  key-groups} settings; pathInfoIsUntrusted only asks the provider
  about signatures a configured group actually requires, so a
  provider need not support every algorithm Nix's native check does

617/617 libstore-tests + 707/707 libutil-tests pass (no regressions).
Real E2E, 6/6 scenarios (measurement/run-oprovider-e2e.sh): legacy
never loads the provider; conjunctive admits on a satisfied group;
conjunctive refuses on an unsatisfiable group; an ABI-version
mismatch is a hard load-time error; a crashing provider segfaults
Nix's own process (exit 139, demonstrated not just asserted -- the
model's defining trade-off); an algorithm the provider can't
evaluate is a hard NIX_SIG_ERROR failure, never silently 'invalid'.
